# Not a full copy -- this is a diff note for the three small, additive
# changes made to the real upstream file ipc/glue/PBackground.ipdl (outside
# this pyxis/ patch directory) to register PPyxisChannel as a PBackground
# managee.
#
# Context / why this file needed to change at all: see
# netwerk/protocol/pyxis/PPyxisChannel.ipdl's own design note (mirrored at
# gecko/patches/pyxis/netwerk/protocol/pyxis/PPyxisChannel.ipdl in this same
# patch tree) for the full reasoning on why PyxisChannel's content-process ->
# parent file-read brokering protocol is `manager PBackground` rather than
# `manager PNecko` or a hand-rolled top-level protocol. Adding ANY new
# manageable protocol to PBackground requires exactly these three additions
# to this one shared file -- there's no way around touching it, but it's a
# purely additive, low-risk change (three one-line insertions, no existing
# lines modified).
#
# 1. Add an `include protocol PPyxisChannel;` line alongside the other
#    `include protocol P*;` lines near the top of the file (inserted after
#    the existing `include protocol PFetch;` / `include protocol
#    PNotification;` lines):
#
#      include protocol PFetch;
#      include protocol PNotification;
#      include protocol PPyxisChannel;
#
# 2. Add a `manages PPyxisChannel;` line inside the `protocol PBackground {`
#    block's manages-list (inserted right after the existing `manages
#    PFetch;` line):
#
#      manages PUDPSocket;
#      manages PVsync;
#      manages PFetch;
#      manages PPyxisChannel;
#
# 3. Add the `async PPyxisChannel();` constructor declaration inside the
#    `parent:` section (inserted right after the existing `async PFetch();`
#    line, before `async RequestCameraAccess(...)`):
#
#      async PFetch();
#
#      async PPyxisChannel();
#
#      async RequestCameraAccess(bool aAllowPermissionRequest) returns (CamerasAccessStatus rv);
#
# PPyxisChannel takes no constructor arguments (mirrors PFetch() above), so
# no additional constructor-arg plumbing is needed here beyond these three
# lines. The corresponding C++ wiring (AllocPPyxisChannelParent -- no
# RecvPPyxisChannelConstructor override needed for a no-arg constructor,
# matching AllocPFetchParent's own pattern) lives in
# ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.h/.cpp -- see the paired .PYXIS_DIFF notes
# for those two files in this same directory.
